## 2. Pokémon Reborn

*Pokémon Reborn* is a fan game by Amethyst and the Reborn development team.
The game itself is **not included in this repository**; obtain it from the
official site.

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `Scripts/**.rb` | Modified source of Pokémon Reborn / Pokémon Essentials. Only the files this patch changes are kept here, not the full tree. |
| `patch/Data/japanese.dat` | The translated message tables. Every entry is keyed by Reborn's original English line, so the file embeds the game's script. |
| `jp_translation/work/src/**`, `work/batch/**`, `work/answers/**` | The same text as editable sources — Reborn's complete English script alongside the translation. |
| `patch/Graphics/**` | Reborn's images with their embedded text repainted in Japanese. Derivative of the original art. |
| `jp_translation/backup/**` | Unmodified copies of Reborn's original scripts and message data, kept so the patch can be reverted. |

Translating and redistributing this material is done on the understanding that
it accompanies, and does not replace, the original game. **Confirm the Reborn
team's position before redistributing.**

## 3. Pokémon

*Pokémon* is a registered trademark of Nintendo, The Pokémon Company, GAME
FREAK and Creatures Inc. The translation uses the **official Japanese names**
of Pokémon, moves, abilities, items and types, and — for entries that exist in
the official games — official Japanese descriptive text. Those rights belong to
the companies above.

`jp_translation/tools/pokeapi_csv/` is **deliberately not committed**. It holds
that official text, and it is only an input to `build_glossary.py` and
`build_descriptions.py`. Both download it on demand from
<https://github.com/PokeAPI/pokeapi> when it is missing.

## 4. Bundled font — `patch/Fonts/pokemonemerald.ttf`

This replaces Reborn's font of the same name, which has no kana or kanji.

It is a merge of two existing faces. Neither is the work of this project.

### Japanese glyphs — PixelMplus / M+ BITMAP FONTS

The name table declares:

    Copyright (C) 2013 M+ Font Project
    Family      PokemonEmerald
    Unique ID   PokemonEmerald;JP
    Version     2013.0602

`2013.0602` is the release date of **PixelMplus 20130602** by itouhiro — a
TrueType outline conversion of **M+ BITMAP FONTS** covering JIS levels 1 and 2.
That is the origin of the kana and kanji.

These are covered by the **M+ FONT LICENSE** (SPDX: `mplus`), the pre-2021 M+
terms, quoted in full:

    M+ FONTS Copyright (C) 2002-2013 M+ FONTS PROJECT

    These fonts are free software.

    Unlimited permission is granted to use, copy, and distribute them, with or
    without modification, either commercially or noncommercially.

    THESE FONTS ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY.

Note that this is the **older** M+ project, hosted at
<https://mplus-fonts.osdn.jp/>. The present-day M+ project at
<https://mplusfonts.github.io/> (M PLUS 1/2, M PLUS Code) is a later,
Google-supported redesign released under the SIL Open Font License, and is
**not** what this font is built from.

- PixelMplus — <https://github.com/itouhiro/PixelMplus>

### Latin glyphs — PokemonEmerald (CC BY-SA 3.0)

The font this one replaces, Reborn's own `Fonts/pokemonemerald.ttf`, declares:

    Copyright aztecwarrior28 2020
    "Pokémon Emerald Pro" by "crystalwalrein", built with FontStruct
    License     Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike
                http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

The bundled font's Latin glyphs are that face. Rasterising `A-Z a-z 0-9` from
both files at 16px produces **byte-identical** output, and the advance widths
match exactly, so the Latin side was carried over rather than redrawn.

- aztecwarrior28, via FontStruct — <https://fontstruct.com/fontstructors/show/1606234/aztecwarrior28>
- crystalwalrein, via FontStruct — <https://fontstruct.com/fontstructors/show/387548/crystalwalrein>

### Consequence

The bundled file states no license of its own, and who merged the two faces is
unknown to this project. Because the Latin glyphs carry CC BY-SA 3.0, the
ShareAlike condition is taken to reach the merged font: it is passed on under
**CC BY-SA 3.0**, with attribution as above. The Japanese glyphs are separately
free under the M+ terms quoted above.

Reborn ships the same CC BY-SA face, so this patch is in the same position as
the game it patches. If you redistribute the font on its own, verify this for
yourself rather than relying on this summary.

